---
// /how — how the studio actually works: the capture loop, told as a field
// manual for people whose heads never go quiet.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const REPO = 'https://github.com/sumit-labz/field-notes';

const steps = [
  {
    n: '01',
    title: 'Keep the pen in your hand',
    body: "Nothing here starts at a desk with a blank page. It starts mid-work: one pen in my hand, a drawing half done, a thought arriving sideways. The rule is simple — don't put the pen down to go and \"write it up properly\". Properly is where thoughts go to die.",
  },
  {
    n: '02',
    title: 'Talk it into Telegram',
    body: "With the free hand, I open Telegram and hold the record button. I talk the way I think: looping, contradicting myself, losing the sentence and finding it again. No one is listening yet. That's the point.",
  },
  {
    n: '03',
    title: 'Photograph the evidence',
    body: 'The sketch, the page of the book, the mess on the table, the screen at 2am. I take pictures like a detective collecting evidence at a scene — not to make them pretty, but to prove the thing happened. Everything goes to the same Telegram bot.',
  },
  {
    n: '04',
    title: 'Let the machine listen',
    body: 'The bot drops each voice note and photo into the archive as a fragment. The voice is transcribed through OpenRouter, and a post is assembled from the pieces — what I said, what I photographed, when.',
  },
  {
    n: '05',
    title: 'Tidy, never rewrite',
    body: "Raw voice gets a clean-verbatim pass: the ums, false starts and repeated words are swept away, but the words, the order and the feeling stay mine. A badge on every voice post says how many words were swept. If it sounds like a press release, the edit went too far.",
  },
  {
    n: '06',
    title: 'Run the loop again',
    body: "Then I go back to work, and the next thought arrives, and I do it again. This is the part I didn't expect: the more I capture my own voice and run it through these loops, the clearer I get about myself. Not because the posts are good — because I can finally hear what I keep saying.",
  },
];
---

<Base title="How it works">
  <p class="how-kicker">a survival guide for overthinkers &amp; ADHDers</p>
  <h1>How this place works</h1>
  <p class="annotation">or: how to get the noise out of your head without stopping what you're doing.</p>

  <p>
    If your head runs eleven tabs at once, you know the problem. The good thought shows up while your hands are busy, and
    by the time you sit down to write it, it's gone — or worse, it's grown into a plan you'll never start. This site is
    my workaround. It isn't a blog I sit down to write. It's a writing system that catches notes on the fly while I build
    my studio; some grow into posts, a few into articles.
  </p>

  <ol class="how-steps">
    {
      steps.map((s) => (
        <li class="how-step" data-reveal>
          <span class="how-step__n">{s.n}</span>
          <h2 class="how-step__title">{s.title}</h2>
          <p>{s.body}</p>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <p class="how-loop" aria-hidden="true">pen → voice → evidence → bot → transcript → tidy → post → ↺</p>

  <p>
    You don't need discipline for this. You need fewer steps between the thought and somewhere safe to put it. One button,
    one bot, one archive. The overthinking still happens — it just happens out loud, on the record, where you can read it
    back later and notice the pattern.
  </p>

  <a class="how-free" href={REPO} rel="noopener">
    <span class="how-free__q">Want this full system for free?</span>
    <span class="how-free__a">Follow the source code <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span>
    <span class="how-free__note">bot, transcription, editing rules, this website — all of it, open on GitHub.</span>
  </a>
</Base>

<style>
  .how-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-meta);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--red);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .how-steps { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 2.5rem 0; }
  .how-step {
    position: relative;
    margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
    padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem 1.1rem 4.2rem;
    border: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 45%, transparent);
    background-color: var(--sheet);
    background-image: var(--tex-grain);
    background-size: 160px;
  }
  .how-step:nth-child(odd) { rotate: -0.4deg; }
  .how-step:nth-child(even) { rotate: 0.5deg; }
  .how-step__n {
    position: absolute;
    left: 1.1rem;
    top: 1.05rem;
    font-family: var(--font-structure);
    font-variation-settings: 'wdth' 62;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-size: 2rem;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--red);
  }
  .how-step__title { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; }
  .how-step p { margin: 0; }
  .how-loop {
    font-family: var(--font-annotation);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--blue);
    text-align: center;
    rotate: -1.5deg;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }
  .how-free {
    display: block;
    margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
    padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    background-image: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    transition: transform var(--dur-settle) var(--ease-paper), box-shadow var(--dur-settle) var(--ease-paper);
  }
  .how-free:hover { transform: translate(-2px, -3px); box-shadow: 4px 5px 0 var(--red); }
  .how-free__q { display: block; font-family: var(--font-display); font-style: italic; font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.2rem); line-height: 1.05; }
  .how-free__a { display: block; margin-top: 0.4rem; font-family: var(--font-meta); font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--red); }
  .how-free__note { display: block; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-family: var(--font-annotation); font-size: 1.15rem; color: var(--graphite); }
</style>
